  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/fundulopanchax_cinnamomeus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Fundulopanchax cinnamomeus reaches about 6 cm in total length. It belongs to the large group of Aphyosemion relatives. Common name: Cinnamon Killi.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/fundulopanchax_cinnamomeus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The species originates from Cameroon.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/fundulopanchax_cinnamomeus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Some of the Aphyosemion (in the largest sense) need rather low water temperatures. Luckily F. cinnamomeus is not demanding in this respect and thrives well at temperatures between 22 and 26°C (best: 23°C). The pH should be in a slightly acidic range.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/fundulopanchax_cinnamomeus_en/",
      "html": "<p>To avoid shy and dull coloured fish the tank should not be lit too brightly and should have a dark gravel; it should also be well planted.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/fundulopanchax_cinnamomeus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The fish feed on any type of fishfood, but prefer frozen and live food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/fundulopanchax_cinnamomeus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Tankmates should never be hectic or aggressive.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/fundulopanchax_cinnamomeus_en/",
      "html": "<p>F. cinnamomeus spawns in the bottom (peat).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/fundulopanchax_cinnamomeus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The longevity of these killis can be compared with that of other fish of the same size; they are not annual.</p><p>Lexicon: Aphyosemion: from ancient Greek, means \"small fish with flag-like fins\". cinnamomeus: means \"coloured like cinnamon\". Fundulopanchax: combined from the generic names Fundulus and Panchax; the name should suggest that the members of the genus show features of both other genera.</p>"
    }
  ],
